contentText:
Katy Perry is speaking out after the White House used her hit song &#8220;Firework&#8221; without her permission.

The 41-year-old pop star took to social media on Saturday (July 25) to condemn the Trump administration for featuring the 2010 anthem in a White House TikTok post showing footage of military strikes. Earlier this week, the White House&#8217;s official TikTok account shared a video that synchronized Perry&#8217;s &#8220;boom, boom, boom&#8221; lyrics with black-and-white footage of bombing. The post was captioned, &#8220;Iran has been warned.&#8221;

